WEBVTT

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.810
<b>Home Run</b>

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.210
Whoa, lookin' good!

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.570
Today's gonna be a good day.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.900
Oh, it's the zero-aim ninja.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.120
It's you... the guy with the dumb face!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.090
You live in Kokura, right?

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.910
Why are you in my batting cages?

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.870
They're not yours!

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.630
If you've got a problem with me, get out!

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.330
I've gotta pay you back for last time!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.380
Pay me back?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.630
Oh, that? Don't worry about it.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.580
You'll just get in my way.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.600
Right to the shortstop. 
That was a double play.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.500
Shut up!

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.400
Ball!

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.320
Ball!

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.270
Ball!

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.530
Ball!

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:56.740
Four balls—rather, four hit-by-pitches—
and the runner advances home.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.050
Shut up or I'll kill you!

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.450
You can't kill me if you don't 
have the aim to hit me.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.580
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:16.140
Damn, why do I keep remembering that?

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.850
Can I help you?

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.810
Hello. Is Zenji here?

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.550
<b>#10  Shortstop</b>

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:57.940
Have some tea.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.280
Thank you.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.130
I called him, so he should be back soon.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.180
This place looks a lot cleaner.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.190
Is that your doing?

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.960
I guess. I cleaned up and had a bath put in.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.170
There's no way I'd live 
somewhere without a bath.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.250
Are you Zenji's boyfriend?

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.860
Like hell.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.540
I'm just a freeloader.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.940
Aren't you Banba's...

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.140
Yes, I'm his ex.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.310
But in truth, I started dating him 
because I was hired to kill him.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:42.260
He's settled down quite a bit now, 
but he was really wild back then.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.490
He partied a lot, so it was 
easy to approach him.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.070
That guy? Really?

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.830
Tell me more—

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.960
Just when the story was getting good...

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.360
I'm home, Lin-chan!

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.380
Where's my "Welcome home"?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.760
Greet our guest first.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.430
You're early, Sayuri-san.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.170
I'm here on time. You're late.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.340
Yeah, sorry.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.270
It's fine.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.020
It gave us time to talk. Right?

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.480
True.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.900
I hope you didn't say anything 
inappropriate, Sayuri-san.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.350
I couldn't say.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:25.610
But anyway, here's what you asked for.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:27.870
What's this?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.790
A list of the Kakyu Association's executives.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.750
I asked her to steal it when 
she assassinated Wang.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.040
Huh.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.540
So what do you want it for?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.750
Isn't that obvious? I'm going to 
take down the Kakyu Association.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:54.770
Um, Lau-san, do people in Hong Kong
always talk business in places like this?

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.420
Of course not.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.950
I don't know my way around Fukuoka,

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.730
so I didn't know where was best 
to have a private conversation.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.290
I see.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:10.080
So, your organization—Sheung Wan, 
was it?—wants to have a presence in Japan.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.480
Yes. Fukuoka's close, so it seems 
like a good place to start.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.540
But there's an organization based 
here that might cause us issues.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.210
The Kakyu Association.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.760
Chairman Wang has been assassinated,

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.850
and the subsequent confusion 
gives us an opportunity to strike.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:32.110
Rumor has it that one of your 
hitmen knows them well.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.670
The Submarine Ninja, I believe.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.600
I can't deny that.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.090
What would you say to signing 
an exclusive contract with us?

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.660
That may be agreeable.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:50.620
Yes, but we would like you 
to prove your mettle.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.950
Could you take out these two men?

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.820
They're Kakyu Association executives.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.860
A test of our capabilities?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.490
Very well.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.860
One more thing, Nitta-san...

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:11.410
I heard the Submarine Ninja is a 
friend of yours from high school.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.560
Yes. Is that an issue?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.330
No, not at all.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:19.660
Do you think I would put 
friendship before business?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:25.400
Not to be rude, but emotions 
may interfere with our business.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.550
Worry not.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:34.180
My assassins, friend or not, 
are nothing but tools to me.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.180
First up is Unoyama Takashi.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.070
His office is in Hakozaki.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:45.570
But it's gonna be a big undertaking, 
killing all of their executives.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.630
Are you sure it's necessary?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.290
The Kakyu Association is still 
after the Niwaka Samurai.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.270
They've been after Sayuri-san 
since she took out Wang, too.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:59.150
And you're still one of their 
targets, too, Lin-chan.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:02.350
Well, that's pretty much
my own doing, after all.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:03.430
Right?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:06.710
I don't think it would hurt you 
to help me out a little.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.740
Fine.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:09.970
What do you need me to do?

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.870
First, change your clothes.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.900
Huh?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:24.550
Hello. I'm Myoken Tatsuro 
from the Myoken Law Firm.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:25.930
And this is my secretary...

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.420
Kobayashi Noriko.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.380
I've been expecting you, Sensei.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:38.720
I'm sorry we arrived so 
far ahead of schedule.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.270
Not at all.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.690
So what I wanted to speak to you about...

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:48.620
I'm having trouble with the 
neighbors and my dogs...

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.150
What is it?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:54.410
Wow... Were those made by Taikei Naotane?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.120
Could I take a closer look?

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:58.820
Yes, please do.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:00.950
I can see you appreciate such things.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.060
How splendid.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:10.090
Aren't they? They weren't easy to come by.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.050
They are splendid forgeries, indeed.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.020
B-Boss!

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.430
Damn!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.270
You have perfect aim, Noriko-san.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.590
Don't call me Noriko-san.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.530
So, who's next?

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.380
A guy who lives in Nishijin: Kim Byonghi.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.410
Who are you?

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.370
A hitman.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.250
You little...

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.750
He was too easy a kill for an executive.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.290
Oh...

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:53.720
Make sure you leave something that shows 
it was you who killed him, Sarucchi.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.260
This is a contract killing, after all.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.350
The Submarine Ninja was here.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.070
Next up is...

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:05.230
Unoyama Takashi in Hakozaki.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.980
What's going on here?

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.170
Looks like something's happened.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.570
Huh? Kim Byonghi?

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:22.290
Yeah, he's one of the 
Kakyu Association's executives.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.130
He's the one we were going to kill.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.670
Right.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:30.100
Hey, don't talk like that in 
front of a police detective.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.090
My bad.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.410
What was the murder weapon?

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.260
We don't have all the details,

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.640
but he was stabbed through the 
heart with something sharp.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.010
Stabbed through the heart?

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:44.450
Oh, and we found a shuriken near the body.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.940
Huh?! What the hell is this?

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.770
Japanese swords?

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.240
S-Sorry I'm so late!

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:59.580
I'm Myoken from the Myoken Law Firm...

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.800
Oh, I didn't kill them.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:05.000
Hey, wait!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.630
Shit. Well, whatever. 
He seemed like a straight-up guy.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.940
How will this play out with the client?

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.050
Kim and Unoyama?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.760
Yes. They were killed in quick succession.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.960
Who did it?

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:28.020
A shuriken was found near both bodies.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:29.740
A shuriken?

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:32.230
You're the Submarine Ninja?

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:37.240
Another organization may have taken him in.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:41.950
Suzuki, escort the other 
executives to a secure location.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:48.480
Then eliminate anyone in the 
organization who seems suspicious.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.210
Yes, sir.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:53.690
To exact our revenge on the 
organization pulling the strings,

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:57.730
we'll need a hitman who can match 
the Submarine Ninja's fighting skill.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:03.270
If that's the case, a broker who isn't 
known to me has requested a meeting.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.510
He knows a Chinese hitman.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.490
He claims he's a skilled fighter.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.430
Are you Suzuki?

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:18.900
You look disappointed that I'm so young.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.280
No, not at all.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:25.810
Don't worry. I might be young, 
but killing is what I do best.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.440
Was our proposed compensation acceptable?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.650
Yeah, but there's one other condition.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.650
I'm looking for this guy.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:41.550
His name is Maomei, 
but he may be using an alias.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:43.510
Ever seen him?

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:45.360
No, I haven't.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.520
I heard he was working for you.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:52.650
One of the executives may be 
employing him on a private basis.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.370
Okay, look into it.

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:58.530
If you find him, I'll do whatever you need.

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:01.330
Your terms are accepted.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.690
But we have some of our own.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:04.200
Yeah, I know.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:07.330
You want me to prove I can do it, right?

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.620
Tell me someone nearby you want dead.

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:16.970
Honestly, I'm really freaked out.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:20.550
They grilled me about whether 
I'd given information to anyone.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:24.130
The executives are all 
hiding away somewhere.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.550
Understood.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.730
I'll hold off on contacting you for a while.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.150
You should lay low, too.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.600
Just one more thing...

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.500
Do you know who was in charge 
of evacuating the executives?

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.570
<b>Fukuya</b>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.570
Thank you very much.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.370
<b>Crossing
Signal</b>

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:17.010
<i>Feilang?</i>

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:30.990
Welcome.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.710
You're connected to an information broker.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.770
I'm not impressed.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.140
Thank you—

00:13:56.780 --> 00:14:01.690
I trusted you... We helped each other...

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:06.360
Did you forget? The only person 
you can trust is yourself.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:10.780
You'd make a lousy hitman, pal.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.150
So long, Mao.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.260
Lin-chan...

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.030
Lin-chan...

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:19.330
Lin!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.370
Were you having a bad dream?

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.340
You were yelling.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:29.210
Sorry.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.060
It's nothing to apologize for.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.310
I'm going out. Will you be okay here?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.640
To kill those executives?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.730
Then I'm coming, too.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:45.230
Actually, the Kakyu Association 
moved faster than I thought.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.450
All the other executives went 
into hiding yesterday.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.290
I see.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:57.850
So I decided to tail Suzuki, 
the guy in charge of the evacuation.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.920
It'll be easier if I go alone.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:04.530
I might need your help again soon, though.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.250
Hope you're up for it.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.590
Okay, I'm off!

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:13.990
Where's my "Have a safe trip"?

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:16.350
Just shut up and go.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.810
So cold.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.540
<i>Banba's handprint...</i>

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.860
<i>He grabbed me really hard, 
but I still didn't wake up.</i>

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.730
<i>If it had been an enemy instead of Banba...</i>

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:39.970
<i>But even Banba...</i>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.660
<i>I'm an idiot.</i>

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.970
<i>I was about to make the same 
mistake I made with Feilang.</i>

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:55.300
<i>I trusted him just because 
he was nice to me.</i>

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.970
<i>I don't know anything about Banba.</i>

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:03.830
<i>There's no guarantee that he's an ally.</i>

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:09.820
<i>I have to end this.</i>

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.080
Thanks for
everything

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.910
Good work last night.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:26.880
Ideally, we would have preferred 
a subtler approach.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.840
You didn't say how to do it.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.090
Well, he certainly looks different.

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:42.390
But that's definitely him.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:46.060
<b>Date of Birth: November 24, 1997 

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.060
So he goes by Lin Xianming now.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:48.940
One of our executives, Zhang, hired him.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:53.300
But Lin killed him and 
disappeared not too long ago.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.500
That's as much as we know.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.830
That's enough.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.490
Do we have a deal?

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:06.580
Yeah, I'll work for your Kakyu Association.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.050
Gross...

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.470
Hello? Can you hear me?

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.930
Perfectly.

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:23.890
How do you like my new weapon, 
the redback spider transmitter?

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:28.820
<i>The range is good, but it feels 
so gross putting it in my ear.</i>

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.320
The target's coming.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.770
He's got a backpack.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.280
Okay, let's try this.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.410
Oh, sorry. Are you okay?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.660
Don't touch me!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.290
Fine.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.460
Oh, it's just a game token.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.410
Mission accomplished.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:56.600
I swiped it like you said.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:57.970
What's in here?

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.190
Congratulations, Yamato.

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:03.010
You just saved Hakata.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:03.810
<i>Huh?</i>

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.110
It's a plastic explosive.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:09.940
He was going to plant it at 
Nakasu-Kawabata Station.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.260
What?!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.900
Tell me that first!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.170
I saw his email and found 
out about his plan.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:24.170
Nakasu-Kawabata's basically 
my backyard, you know?

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.660
I don't want anyone causing a ruckus there.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:30.740
Lin-kun! Perfect timing.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:32.150
I need a favor...

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.550
Why do you have a suitcase?

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.820
Are you running away from home?

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:39.330
Idiot! What are you talking about?

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.970
I don't have a home!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.420
Wait... You are?

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.660
Why?

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:46.680
Did you and Banba-san have a fight?

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.660
Just leave it!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.640
But I wanna know! Did something happen?

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:53.440
Going through a rebellious phase, at your age?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.030
If you don't tell me, I'll call your home.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.120
What?

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.300
Sarucchi, where are you? Still in Hakata?

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.130
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.290
Good.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:18.340
Can you head over to Hakata 
Wharf as fast as you can?

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:21.180
Hakata Wharf? Why?

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:25.890
It's about that Sheung Wan organization.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:30.700
Their drug stash at the 
wharf is under attack.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.860
What the hell are you thinking?

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:39.970
You wanted to distract Sheung Wan, didn't you?

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:44.840
You knew it was these guys who were
planning to kill the executives, right?

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:48.730
Yes, but this is more than a distraction.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.040
It's a declaration of war!

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.420
No need to worry.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.980
I'll finish up properly.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.230
Hey.

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:58.550
Put the two survivors in the car.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:03.090
Hey, what are you doing?

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.220
We're leaving.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.710
I can take some spoils, can't I?

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:12.890
Well, hurry it up.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.700
Like I said, something was just wrong.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.200
What does that mean?

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:34.270
I mean, someone like you 
has a clear objective.

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:37.760
You work for the money, 
and good and evil don't enter into it.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.460
Thanks for the compliment.

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:41.890
But Banba isn't like that.

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.720
I don't know what he's thinking.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.800
I've let myself become vulnerable.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.640
Oh, I see.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:55.020
So you ran away because you 
didn't want him to betray you.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.400
It's not about that.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.490
I was just starting to get a little 
too pampered by that life.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.540
What's wrong with that?

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.930
People like us don't get 
to die pleasant deaths.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:12.950
So I think it's fine to just enjoy 
being pampered while you can.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:18.320
So what was this favor you wanted?

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.920
Ah, I just got in.

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:23.060
Who's that?

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:26.170
Our spy at the Kakyu Association.

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.640
He was killed last night.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.420
I feel responsible.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:33.900
We have other spies, but...

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:38.980
I'd like you to kill him before 
he does the same to them.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.980
I see. So that's it.

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:45.300
Hey, show me his face again!

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:46.900
Okay.

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.420
It can't be...

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:56.840
Huh? Don't tell me you know him.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:59.260
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.590
That's Feilang.

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:06.050
My best friend who killed me six years ago.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:09.760
You killed them, huh?

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.230
So what if I did?

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:14.300
I'll kill you.

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:10.170
Such a damn wet blanket...

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:15.080
In that case, I'll destroy them.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
#11  Brawl
